From e09a4f33779a9c43547630c25b5e87390c5bbaa1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:37:14 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 07/13] drm/asahi: g17: m5: build the 27.3 beta 1 (26C5035r) HW
 data

The M5 firmware of macOS 27.3 beta 1 (26C5035r, RTKit pac-3514.60.8)
takes the 26B123 version word and allocation sizes (its kext writes the
same root+0 word at AGXG17X 0xfffffe0008bd0dfc..0xfffffe0008bd0e0c and
keeps the same u64[24] at __TEXT,__const 0xfffffe0007153188), but its
HW data is not 26B123's: one u32 is inserted at 0x2720 and every later
field moves by 4. Its kext stores at 0x2724 (8 zero bytes), 0x272c,
0x2730, 0x2734, ..., the kick-shared pointer at 0x27e0, ..., 0x284a
where the 26A428 and 26B123 kexts store at 0x2720, 0x2728, 0x272c,
0x2730, ..., 0x27dc, ..., 0x2846; the 314 stores below 0x2720 are the
same. The version word does not tell the two builds apart; only the
firmware identity does.

The new word is the time the firmware waits for the GPU to reach a
forced idle after a sleep request, in ms. The 26C5035r G17S firmware
loads it at TEXT 0x29e18 (ldr w22, [x8, #0x2720]), skips the wait when
it is 0, compares it times 24000 ticks with the time since the request
and then reports "GPU did not reach forced idle within %ums of the
sleep request"; the 26B123 firmware has neither the load nor the
message. The kext computes it at AGXG17X 0xfffffe0008bd0644..
0xfffffe0008bd0660 from word 0x284 of the accelerator, times 1000,
saturating to 0xffffffff from 0x418938 on (mul, cmp, csinv).

The value 5000 is inferred, not read from a running macOS: word 0x284
is IOGPU's waitForGPUTimeoutSeconds, IOGPUFamily's configuration
defaults (0xfffffe000aa85ba0) set it to 5 from __const
0xfffffe0007a71250 + 0xc, and neither AGXG17X nor IOGPUFamily's
boot-argument parsing stores to it.

Describe the move with the layout bands the HW data already uses
(M5_26C5035_HW_DATA_BANDS: 0..0x2720 stays, 0x2720..0x284c moves by
4; the four bytes it drops past 0x284c are zero in the 26A428
encoding), apply them after the 26A428 encoding and write the word,
and find the kick-shared pointer and the enabled-core words through
them. Add RootProfile J714G17S26C5035, M5Layouts::V26C5035 and its
Variant V26C5035_M5, and have the 27.3 (26C5035r) G17S build of the
M5 Pro name it instead of V26B123_M5. The fwid KUnit test that checks
each M5 Pro build's layouts follows.

check_layout.py relocates the 26B123 kext's HW data store bytes from
0x2700 on by the bands and gets exactly the 26C5035r kext's, and finds
the encoded 26C5035r HW data of every board equal to the 26A428
encoding below 0x2720, 5000 at 0x2720 and the 26A428 bytes
0x2720..0x284c at 0x2724.

The check scripts are in contrib/validated/aurora/prs/gpu-27.2/checks/
of https://github.com/rolotrealanis98/m5pro-linux.

Signed-off-by: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: LLM Claude
